# Allowlist for tools/docs_private_info_lint.py. One entry per line:
#   path <exact path>  skip that one tracked file (wildcards are rejected, so no whole
#                      directory or scope root can be switched off)
#   value <literal>    accept this exact matched string anywhere
# Every entry REQUIRES a '# reason' (missing reason is a usage error). Never list real
# household data.
# SCOPE: the lint scans docs ONLY (docs/**, README.md, .trail/learnings/**), not code/fixtures.
# DECISION: MACs with the 02:00:00 prefix (locally administered dummy) and the IANA
# documentation range 00:00:5E:00:53 are always allowed: the repo's fixtures and README use
# 02:00:00:xx:xx:xx as dummy devices. Other locally-administered MACs are NOT exempt, since
# phones use randomised ones.

path .trail/learnings/2026-10-25-claude-owns-dhcp-option-order-parser-bearyjd.md  # historical learning, immutable; `user` is a generic account name
path .trail/learnings/2026-10-25-codex-closeout-frozen-gui-candidate-released-codex.md  # historical learning, immutable; `user` is a generic account name

value 192.168.1.1        # OpenWrt factory-default router address, used as the example router in docs/spikes/ and docs/deployment-validation-*.md
value 192.168.8.1        # GL.iNet factory-default router address (README states it is the default)
value 192.168.8.0        # GL.iNet factory-default LAN prefix (192.168.8.0/24), the documented default LAN set in docs/spikes/conntrack-helper.md
value 192.168.8.10       # example server/record host inside the GL.iNet default subnet (README, docs/spikes/conntrack-helper.md); keeps router/server/control host in one subnet
value 192.168.8.50       # example control-app host inside the GL.iNet default subnet (README firewall section)
value 10.9.9.9           # unassigned test address recorded in a measurement in docs/spikes/p1-collector-net.md
value 192.168.1.50       # synthetic e2e fixture host documented in docs/e2e.md (matches tests/e2e data)
value c2:11:22:33:44:01  # synthetic e2e fixture MAC range documented in docs/e2e.md (matches tests/e2e data)
